data: {"kind": "tool_call", "agent": "analyst", "name": "run_query", "args": {"query": "SELECT\n    scene_number,\n    slugline,\n    kind,\n    summary,\n    script_excerpt\nFROM retention.scenes\nWHERE\n    episode = 4\n    AND scene_number IN (12, 13)\nORDER BY scene_number\n"}}

data: {"kind": "tool_result", "agent": "analyst", "name": "run_query", "preview": "{\"columns\": [\"scene_number\", \"slugline\", \"kind\", \"summary\", \"script_excerpt\"], \"rows\": [[12, \"INT. KELLEHER HOUSE - PORCH - NIGHT\", \"reveal\", \"June confesses: she saw the boat that night from the porch. She saw two boats. She went back to bed.\", \"JUNE: I saw two boats. I saw his and I saw the other one and I went back to bed, Nora. I went back to bed.\"], [13, \"INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - NIGHT\", \"exposition\", \"Gil lays out the entire dredging permit history: the 2019 application, the environmental review, the quota transfer clause, who signed what and when.\", \"GIL: The 2019 application was denied. Then in 2021 it comes back with a quota transfer clause nobody asked for. Now look at the environmental review \\u2014 see the date? Same week the county changed assessors. And here \\u2014\"]]}"}

data: {"kind": "tool_call", "agent": "analyst", "name": "run_query", "args": {"query": "SELECT\n    s.scene_number,\n    s.slugline,\n    s.summary,\n    sum(h.seeks) AS total_seeks\nFROM retention.seek_heatmap AS h\nJOIN retention.scenes AS s ON h.episode = s.episode AND h.to_bucket * 10 BETWEEN s.start_sec AND s.end_sec\nWHERE\n    h.episode = 4\n    AND h.backward = 1\n    AND h.to_bucket > 0\nGROUP BY\n    s.scene_number,\n    s.slugline,\n    s.summary\nORDER BY total_seeks DESC\nLIMIT 5\n"}}

data: {"kind": "tool_result", "agent": "analyst", "name": "run_query", "preview": "{\"columns\": [\"scene_number\", \"slugline\", \"summary\", \"total_seeks\"], \"rows\": [[13, \"INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - NIGHT\", \"Gil lays out the entire dredging permit history: the 2019 application, the environmental review, the quota transfer clause, who signed what and when.\", 290], [4, \"INT. BAIT SHOP - DAY\", \"Tess gives Nora a dashcam SD card from her father's truck. She hasn't watched it.\", 227], [6, \"EXT. HARBOR - DAY\", \"Gil identifies the truck. It's registered to the sheriff's office.\", 208], [3, \"INT. KELLEHER HOUSE - DAY\", \"Nora tells Walt what Gil did. Walt says Gil is the only honest man in town.\", 176], [5, \"INT. NORA'S ROOM - DAY\", \"The dashcam: the truck at the dock at 11:40pm. Two men carrying something to the water.\", 145]]}"}

data: {"kind": "text", "agent": "analyst", "text": "Episode 4 loses the most viewers during a long exposition scene about dredging permits, which causes a 2.7% retention drop in the minute leading up to second 2589.\n\nThis is a **story problem**. The drop-off is caused by a sudden shift in pacing. A scene with a major emotional reveal is immediately followed by a long, dry scene explaining complex administrative details. The audience is coming from a moment of high drama and is then presented with a dense, nine-minute exposition.\n\nHowever, it's worth noting that this same scene is also the most rewatched part of the episode. This suggests that the information is important, but its delivery is alienating a segment of the audience.\n\n### The Scene\nThe drop-off happens in Scene 13, which comes right after Scene 12's confession.\n\n*   **Scene 12 (Preceding)**: `INT. KELLEHER HOUSE - PORCH - NIGHT` (reveal)\n    *   **Summary**: June confesses: she saw the boat that night from the porch. She saw two boats. She went back to bed.\n    *   **Excerpt**: `JUNE: I saw two boats. I saw his and I saw the other one and I went back to bed, Nora. I went back to bed.`\n*   **Scene 13 (Problem)**: `INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - NIGHT` (exposition)\n    *   **Summary**: Gil lays out the entire dredging permit history: the 2019 application, the environmental review, the quota transfer clause, who signed what and when.\n    *   **Excerpt**: `GIL: The 2019 application was denied. Then in 2021 it comes back with a quota transfer clause nobody asked for. Now look at the environmental review \u2014 see the date? Same week the county changed assessors. And here \u2014`\n\n### Rewatch Hotspots\nThe most rewatched scenes are all moments of discovery and revelation, where key pieces of the mystery are uncovered.\n\n1.  **Scene 13**: `INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - NIGHT` - Gil explains the permit history.\n2.  **Scene 4**: `INT. BAIT SHOP - DAY` - Tess gives Nora the dashcam SD card.\n3.  **Scene 6**: `EXT. HARBOR - DAY` - Gil identifies the truck as belonging to the sheriff's office.\n4.  **Scene 3**: `INT. KELLEHER HOUSE - DAY` - Nora learns from Walt that Gil is the only honest man in town.\n5.  **Scene 5**: `INT. NORA'S ROOM - DAY` - The dashcam footage reveals two men carrying something to the water.\n\n### Data\n"}

